        "content": "## How to use this dashboard\n\n1. **Run a load test** using one of the k6 scripts in `tests/load/`.\n2. **Archive the result** with `node tests/load/lib/results.js archive <scenario> <result.json> [db_size]`.\n3. **Check for regressions** with `node tests/load/regression_check.js <scenario> <result.json>` or `node tests/load/lib/baseline.js compare <scenario> <result.json>`.\n4. **View trends** with `node tests/load/lib/results.js trend <scenario> --last 10`.\n5. **Promote a new baseline** after an intentional improvement: `node tests/load/lib/baseline.js promote <scenario> <result.json> [db_size]`.\n\n### Regression thresholds (from `baselines.json`)\n\n| Metric type | Threshold |\n|---|---|\n| Latency (p50/p95/p99) | > 20% above baseline |\n| Error rate | > 2 percentage points above baseline |\n| Memory growth (soak) | > 50% above baseline |\n\nSee [docs/load-testing-runbook.md](https://github.com/Soroban-Pulse/SorobanPulse/blob/main/docs/load-testing-runbook.md) for the full runbook.",
